{{Quote|Slavery is the natural order of things. The weak deserve nothing more than to kneel before the strong, bound to our service.|Queen Miraj Scintel|audio=Zygerrian2.flac|<ref name="Slaves of the Republic" />}}
The '''Zygerrian Slave Empire''', known as the '''Zygerrian Empire''', was an [[Politics|empire]] of the [[Zygerrian]] [[species]] located inside the [[Outer Rim Territories]] of [[the galaxy]]. From their [[capital]] of [[Zygerria]], a vast [[slavery]] industry for thousands of years was maintained before the [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] declared it illegal and the [[Jedi Order]] [[Jedi–Zygerrian conflict|fought and dismantled]] their slaving operations and left the empire shattered.

During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Queen of Zygerria|Queen]] [[Miraj Scintel]] wished to restore the ancient slavery industry as part of a plot with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and its [[Head of State|leader]] [[Count]] [[Dooku]]. The two governments [[Conquest of Kiros|dispatched]] forces to the [[Togruta]] colony world of [[Kiros]], and captured the local population. However, their plans were foiled by the [[Jedi]] who located the missing colonists, while their [[queen]] was killed by Dooku.

Understanding that the laws concerning slavery could be [[Imperial Era|different under]] the [[Galactic Empire]], the slaver known as [[Raney]], who along with his [[troop]]s, took advantage of the Republic's [[Proclamation of the New Order|fall]] and sought a return to [[Kadavo]], hoping to flourish once more. 

By the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[King]] [[Atai Molec]] ascended to the throne and his heir, [[Prince]] [[Sono Molec]], assumed control of [[Kowak]]. The two began to resurrect the Zygerrian Empire to its full glory.

==History==
===Prospering and defeat===
{{Quote|For thousands of years, Zygerria supplied slave labor to the galaxy. We prospered. Our customers prospered. Then the Jedi came.|Darts D'Nar|<ref name="Kidnapped">{{TCW|Kidnapped}}</ref>}}
[[File:ZygerrianSellingSlave.png|thumb|210x210px|A Zygerrian presents a prisoner to potential buyers.]]
The [[Zygerrian]] slavers successfully maintained their slave industry for thousands of years, which supplied slave labor to unscrupulous masters in the galaxy who were wealthy and powerful. At its height, the population of Zygerria built fortresses and cities on top of the mesas scattered throughout the planet, using their slaves. However, it would fade from its glory after the [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] declared slavery illegal, the [[Jedi]] [[Jedi–Zygerrian conflict|cracked]] down on their slaving operations and liberated countless beings from bondage. This action ended the slavery the Zygerrians excelled in, pushing it into the shadows of the underworld, dismantling the empire, and confining what was left of its government to [[Zygerria]], the civilization's [[homeworld]].<ref name="DB Zygerrian" />

During the [[High Republic Era]], the [[Zygerrian Alliance]] existed, which continued slaving operations. The future [[Nihil]] [[Tempest Runner]] [[Lourna Dee]] was among their slaves, but she was freed by a joint Jedi&ndash;Republic [[Attack on the Zygerrian camp|attack]] on an [[Unidentified Zygerrian camp|alliance camp]].<ref name="Tempest Runner">''[[The High Republic: Tempest Runner]]''</ref>

===Restoration===
{{Quote|My queen is going to bring back the royal slave auction as in the days before the Jedi. Zygerria will be rich and powerful again.|Darts D'Nar|audio=Zygerrian7.flac|<ref name="Kidnapped" />}}
During the late [[Republic Era]], the Zygerrians maintained slave-run work colonies.<ref name="TPM-25th">[[The Phantom Menace 25th Anniversary Special 1|''The Phantom Menace'' 25th Anniversary Special 1]]</ref> with [[Queen]] [[Miraj Scintel]] seeing an opportunity to renew Zygerria's ancient slave trade and developed a plot to gain the aid of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and its [[Head of State]], [[Count]] [[Dooku]] during the [[Clone Wars]], . Dispatching the Zygerrian Commander [[Darts D'Nar]] to the Togruta colony world of [[Kiros]]<ref name="Kidnapped" /> in a [[Conquest of Kiros|conquest]],<ref name="Darts Databank">{{Databank|darts-dnar|Darts D'Nar}}</ref> D'Nar and his forces moved in to "occupy" the colony. Dooku had convinced the governor, [[Gupat Roshti]], to be taken to a "safe haven," only for [[battle droid]]s<ref name="Kidnapped" /> and Zygerrian slavers to take the population away.<ref name="Cody Bio Gallery">{{Databank|clone-commander-cody-biography-gallery|Clone Commander Cody Biography Gallery}} {{C|Slide 18}}</ref> When the Republic responded and a [[battle on Kiros]] began, Dooku and Zygerrian [[Prime minister (Zygerria)|Prime Minister]] [[Atai Molec]] then contacted him as he negotiated with, and later fought, [[Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]. Dooku then ordered D'Nar to bring Kenobi to him on his knees, but the incident ended in D'Nar's capture. The Confederacy supplied the Zygerrians with the captured Togruta population, whom the Zygerrians hoped to sell by bringing back the royal slave auction, a tradition of the old Empire.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

[[File:AgrussWelcomesKenobi-SotR.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Agruss welcomes Kenobi to his "education center"]]
However, their plans were foiled by the [[Jedi]] who located the missing colonists, and sent [[Jedi Knight]]s [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], and [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]], who was a Togruta, undercover to [[Mission to Zygerria|infiltrate]] the slavers' auction on Zygerria, where Skywalker and Tano posed as master and slave. Tano later threatened Scintel, but the queen had already outfitted the girl's neck with a [[shock collar]], which she then remotely activated, electrocuting Tano unconscious. Skywalker and Kenobi were captured too.<ref name="Slaves of the Republic" /> At this point, Scintel started developing feelings for Skywalker and decided not to kill him which Molec saw as a weakness and invited Dooku to Zygerria to speak with the Queen about her defiance in not killing Skywalker. When the Queen refused to kill him, again, Molec and Dooku decided to take matters into their own hands, seeing Scintel unfit to be queen. Molec then stood by, watching, as Dooku Force-choked her. However, she was saved by the timely arrival of Skywalker, who tried to convince [[Miraj Scintel]] that she too was a slave and pawn in the Separatists plot, something she realized to be true just before succumbing to her injuries and dying while escaping in the hands of Skywalker.<ref name="Escape from Kadavo">{{TCW|Escape from Kadavo}}</ref>

With the queen dead<ref name="Escape from Kadavo" /> and Atai Molec having taken her place as ruler,<ref name="Friends">''[[Friends Like These]]''</ref> Skywalker and Tano escaped from the Zygerrians and headed for Kadavo to rescue Kenobi, Rex, and the Togruta captives, who had been transferred to the [[Kadavo slave processing facility|Zygerrian slave processing facility]] on the planet. While en route, the two also called for reinforcements from the Republic.<ref name="Escape from Kadavo" />

Tano and her Master soon arrived on the planet onboard the [[YV-865 Aurore-class freighter|YV-865 ''Aurore''-class freighter]] ''[[Tecora]]'' and tried to break into the slave processing facility. When ordered to cease by the Zygerrian [[Keeper]] [[Agruss]] under threat that the slaves would be [[Death|killed]], Skywalker did not comply. Later when [[Galactic Republic]] reinforcements led by [[Admiral]] [[Barton Coburn]] and Jedi Master [[Plo Koon]] landed on [[Kadavo]], they [[Battle of Kadavo|confronted]] the slavers, with the [[104th Battalion|Wolfpack]] detachment attacking the facility with [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|LAAT/i gunships]] and [[clone Z-95 starfighter]]s. However, although they were initially halted by its [[ray shield]]s, Skywalker was able to destroy the defensive towers. Meanwhile, Kenobi and Rex rebelled and killed Agruss who, in a last act, tried to throw the Togruta hostages into the volcanic crevice below the facility, but following a plan devised by Tano, the Republic forces evacuated everyone onto Admiral Coburn's [[Arquitens-class light cruiser|''Arquitens''-class light cruiser]] ''[[Hand of Justice]]''. The Republic strike team then destroyed the slave facility, with its destruction dealing a crippling blow to the Zygerrian slave trade. After their escape, the Togruta gladly joined the Republic.<ref name="Escape from Kadavo" />

===Rebuilding===
{{Quote|With the meddling Republic gone, we can return to Kadavo and rebuild what was taken from us. Under this new empire, our operation will flourish once again.|Raney|<ref name="Rampage">{{TBB|Rampage (episode)}}</ref>}}
Despite the defeat of the Separatist-aligned Zygerrian slave trade,<ref name="Escape from Kadavo" /> a Zygerrian named [[Raney]] came to command a group of slavers; which were made up of a [[YV-865 Aurore-class freighter|YV-865 ''Aurore''-class freighter]]<ref name="Rampage">{{TBB|Rampage (episode)}}</ref> and an encampment<ref name="Raney">{{Databank|raney|Raney}}</ref>&ndash;staffed by Zygerrian soldiers and his pet [[Brezak]]&mdash;in the ruins of [[Old Ord Mantell City]] on the planet of [[Ord Mantell]].<ref name="Rampage" /> The Clone Wars would also come to an [[Mission to Mustafar|end]], as the Confederacy collapsed after the deaths of its leaders, while the Republic was [[Proclamation of the New Order|transformed]] into the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Understanding that the laws concerning slavery could be different under a new regime,<ref name="Rampage" /> Raney and his [[troop]]s took advantage of the Republic's fall, taking captives to build a new empire. Their prisoners included [[human]]s and [[Falleen]], who were made into their slaves,<ref name="Raney" /> and an adolescent rancor named [[Muchi]], which had belonged to [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]].<ref name="Rampage" />

[[File:BadBatchAmbushed-Rampage.png|thumb|right|250px|The Bad Batch was captured by Zygerrian slavers.]]
Raney sought to return to Kadavo<ref name="Raney" /> to make up for their defeat during the Clone Wars. Meanwhile, desperate for the return of his pet, Jabba had his [[majordomo]], [[Bib Fortuna]], hire the [[Trandoshan]] [[Ciddarin Scaleback|Cid]] to rescue the rancor; Cid hired a team of deserting [[clone commando]]s named [[Clone Force 99]], otherwise called "the Bad Batch," to rescue Muchi from the slavers, albeit without informing them Muchi was a rancor. Ordering their youngest member&mdash;the enhanced [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]]&mdash;to stay back at their ship, the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|''Marauder'']], the [[commando]]s attempted to attack the encampment, only for the Brezak to attack [[Echo|CT-1409]] "Echo," revealing the presence of the team. The commandos were captured to be made into slaves, and two Zygerrian guards searched through the ''Marauder'' but found nothing, as Omega remained hidden and [[GNK-series power droid]] [[Gonky (Clone Force 99)|Gonky]] pretended to simply be a box. Seeing that her friends were captured, Omega set out to rescue them, being caught only after she removed the lock on Muchi's cage and rampaged throughout the encampment, allowing the Bad Batch to rescue the slaves. As Echo and Omega escorted them to safety and while Muchi fought the Brezak, [[Clone Sergeant]] "[[Hunter]]" fought Raney, who attacked the commando with his [[electro-whip]]. Nevertheless, Hunter overcame the pain and quickly defeated the slaver. Afterward, Omega would claim a [[Omega's Zygerrian energy bow|Zygerrian energy bow]], and clone commando "[[Wrecker]]" began to fight Muchi in order to convince the rancor to follow them. With the Zygerrians defeated, the Bad Batch was able to escort Muchi back to [[Cid's Parlor]], where she was reunited with Fortuna.<ref name="Rampage" /> 

By the [[Galactic Civil War]], Molec had ascended to the throne and his son [[Prince]] [[Sono Molec]] assumed control of the Zygerrian outpost on [[Kowak]] from [[Molec Royal Palace|his palace]].<ref name="FLT" />

==Organization==
===Government===
{{Main|Queen of Zygerria|Prime minister (Zygerria)}}
[[File:Unidentified_Zygerrian_royal_guard_3.png|thumb|left|200px|A Zygerrian royal guard, a class of soldier who served as protection throughout Zygerrian markets and facilities.]]
The Zygerrian Empire was ruled by a [[king]]<ref name="FLT" />, or [[Queen of Zygerria|queen]] as the sovereign ruler. Aiding the ruler was the [[Prime minister (Zygerria)|prime minister]], who wielded considerable powers and additionally was the [[Captain of the Guard]] of the [[Zygerrian Royal Guard|royal guards]], a group of [[Soldier|sentinels]] sworn to protect Zygerria's [[Queen]]. These positions thereby collectively form into one common order, and controlling the [[slavery]] industry, making the Zygerrian Empire wealthy and powerful but at the expense of others.<ref name="Slaves of the Republic" /><ref name="DB Atai Molec" />

===Outside relations===
Diplomatically, the Zygerrians were highly corporate-minded who sought to maintain their empire at the expense of other civilizations, holding countless slaves across many worlds across the galaxy. This became a valuable part of Zygerrian culture and heritage.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

==Society and culture==
{{Main|Zygerrian}}
{{Quote|How can a civilization this advanced still practice slavery?''"<br />"''It makes them wealthy and powerful at the expense of others.|Ahsoka Tano and Anakin Skywalker, on the Zygerrians|<ref name="Slaves of the Republic" />}}
Cunning, the [[Zygerrian]]s were a [[humanoid]] [[feline]] [[species]] that were a warlike and selfish minded race who held in great esteem that it was the natural order of life for the strong to dominate the weak, so slavery was normal for the species, and that all were bound to their service, to that they showed a large amount of [[Xenophobia|prejudice]] towards [[alien]]s and [[human]]s alike.<ref name="Kidnapped" />

==Astrography==
The ancient Zygerrian Slave Empire stretched far and wide, and presided over countless [[sector]]s right across [[the galaxy]], but was eventually pushed back by the [[Jedi]] Order to [[Zygerria]].<ref name="DB Zygerrian" />

During the [[Republic Era|time]] of [[Clone Wars]], the Zygerrian Slave Empire reappeared on Zygerria as it was during the ancient era.<ref name="Slaves of the Republic" /> It came to control the [[Togruta]] colony world of [[Kiros]], located in the [[Expansion Region]],<ref name="Kidnapped" /> as well as [[Kadavo]], which was located in [[Wild Space]].<ref name="Escape from Kadavo" /> By the [[Imperial Era]], it ruled [[Kowak]] in the Outer Rim.<ref name="FLT" />

